Here's a tidy prime checker for you! ✨
```swift
func isPrime(_ n: Int) -> Bool {
    if n < 2 { return false }
    var i = 2
    while i * i <= n {
        if n % i == 0 { return false }
        i += 1
    }
    return true
}
```
The trick that keeps it quick: it only tests divisors **up to the square root of n**, so it never wastes time on the bigger ones.

Leap years have a sneaky little rule, so here's the neat version:
```python
def is_leap(year):
    return year % 4 == 0 and (year % 100 != 0 or year % 400 == 0)
```
In plain words: divisible by 4, **except century years**, which must also be divisible by 400. 📅
